redfin 1210: SweetMesa ends a pre-empted op (3/4/38 while an op runs) with its *Cancelled status; op-end FIFO; kern.sweet_mesa_fix

BiometricSupport starts a new op without cancelling the running one, so the pre-empted op stayed at
activeBioOpsQueue[0] and every later status/match went to its dead client (SpringBoard never saw its lock-screen
match). 1203s gEndPend bitmask is replaced by an ordered queue (two ends of one kind give two statuses); queued ends
are delivered from the thread call after the command block and before any translated sweetfpcd event.
kern.sweet_mesa_fix (default 0x7): bit 0 this fix, bit 1 1211, bit 2 1212, bit 3 1213. kern.sweet_mesa_fix_stats.
Klog: "implicit op end delivered: old <kind> op, status 0x.. (..), new cmd N <name>".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
